            <ArticleTitle>Colonic Perforation: A Medical Complication.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>100-104</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.14712/23362936.2017.10</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hypothyroidism is a common comorbidity that on acute presentation is often overlooked. It can be an easily managed condition; however non-compliance can have severe consequences. In the presented case it was requirement for emergency surgery that resulted in stoma formation. This case is a first example of the need to include patient's decision making process with regards to medication adherence in the setting of chronic disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
